==English==

===Etymology===
1896, American, {{suffix|feist|t1=small, aggressive dog|y}};<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> the term {{term|feist|lang=en}} (now rare) itself originally meant “stink”, and earlier “fart”, from {{etyl|enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic}}, presumably from {{proto|Indo-European}} – see {{term|feist|lang=en}} for details.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|aɪsti}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|feist|ier|more}}

# [[tenacious|Tenacious]], [[energetic]], [[spunky]].
# [[belligerent|Belligerent]]; prepared to [[stand]] and [[fight]], especially in spite of relatively small [[stature]] or some other [[disadvantage]]. 
#  Easily [[offend]]ed and ready to [[bicker]].

====Derived terms====
* [[feistily]]
* [[feistiness]]

